<speak>I am comfortable here; the door is already closed. My family knows I am on a call. They have become better at respecting time set aside for things, although I am probably the person who needs the most reminding. I used to answer business messages during dinner without thinking. Now, when I tell everyone that I am stepping back, they quite reasonably ask why I am still looking at the phone. It is easier to announce a change than to stop reaching for the same habits.</speak>